{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UZuKTYEzamZZScFkhcD7H6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Design: Extend Minimal Operational Observability\n2\t\n3\t**Issue:** QuantAgent-s62  \n4\t**Related:** [RQ](../01_requirements/QuantAgent-s62-RQ-operational-observability.md) | [PL](../02_planning/QuantAgent-s62-PL-operational-observability.md) | [AC](../05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-s62-AC-operational-observability.md)\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Level of Detail\n9\t\n10\t**STANDARD** — UI-layer wiring of existing primitives; no new persistence or models required.\n11\t\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t## Affected Components\n15\t\n16\t- `quantagent/llm_telemetry.py` — new aggregation function\n17\t- `apps/streamlit/services/db.py` — new DbHandle method\n18\t- `apps/streamlit/views/dashboard.py` — wire placeholder\n19\t- `apps/streamlit/views/paper_trading.py` — two new sections\n20\t- `apps/streamlit/views/logs.py` — environment filter\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## Design Decisions\n25\t\n26\t### DD1 — Reuse existing primitives, no new tables\n27\t\n28\t`QuantAgent-69d` already persists `llm_call` log rows with `environment`, `extra_data` (tokens, duration), and `event_type`. The new `get_environment_metrics()` function filters on these fields. This requires no migrations.\n29\t\n30\t`QuantAgent-vje` already defines `SchedulerHeartbeat` model and `DbHandle.get_latest_heartbeat()`. The dashboard wiring is pure UI: replace placeholder text with a call to the existing method.\n31\t\n32\t### DD2 — `get_environment_metrics()` in `llm_telemetry.py`\n33\t\n34\t```python\n35\tdef get_environment_metrics(\n36\t    db: Any,\n37\t    environment: str,\n38\t    hours_back: int = 24,\n39\t) -> dict[str, Any]:\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\t- Queries `Log` rows: `event_type='llm_call'`, `environment=environment`, `timestamp >= now - hours_back hours`.\n43\t- Delegates to `_aggregate_rows()` (reuse existing).\n44\t- Returns same shape as `get_session_metrics()`: `{calls, input_tokens_sum, output_tokens_sum, total_tokens_sum, duration_ms_sum, duration_ms_avg, by_operation}`.\n45\t\n46\t### DD3 — `DbHandle.get_paper_llm_metrics()`\n47\t\n48\tThin wrapper in `db.py` to keep the view layer clean:\n49\t\n50\t```python\n51\tdef get_paper_llm_metrics(self, environment: str, hours_back: int = 24) -> dict:\n52\t    if not self.ok:\n53\t        return {}\n54\t    try:\n55\t        from quantagent.llm_telemetry import get_environment_metrics\n56\t        with self.SessionLocal() as session:\n57\t            return get_environment_metrics(session, environment, hours_back)\n58\t    except Exception:\n59\t        return {}\n60\t```\n61\t\n62\t### DD4 — Dashboard scheduler status wiring\n63\t\n64\tThe Dashboard's \"Scheduler Status\" placeholder gets replaced with an inline snippet that calls `db.get_latest_heartbeat(environment)` and renders status/last-run. Helper functions `_calculate_status()` and `_humanize_time()` are duplicated inline (3 lines each) in dashboard.py to avoid creating a shared utils file for this single usage — consistent with AGENTS.md \"minimum needed for the current task.\"\n65\t\n66\t### DD5 — Paper Trading tab extensions\n67\t\n68\tTwo new `st.divider()` + section blocks are appended after the existing `_render_recent_runs()` call in `render()`:\n69\t\n70\t**Block A — Positions, Orders & PnL:**\n71\t```\n72\t[Divider]\n73\tst.subheader(\"Positions & Orders\")\n74\t  col: open positions table (Position model — all, no env filter)\n75\t  col: recent orders table (Order filtered by environment, limit 20)\n76\t[Divider]\n77\tst.subheader(\"PnL Summary\")\n78\t  unrealized PnL from positions\n79\t  daily realized PnL from trades (today, filtered by environment)\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\t**Block B — LLM Cost & Latency:**\n83\t```\n84\t[Divider]\n85\tst.subheader(\"LLM Cost & Latency (last 24h)\")\n86\t  metrics = db.get_paper_llm_metrics(environment)\n87\t  if metrics.get(\"calls\", 0) == 0:\n88\t      st.info(\"No LLM telemetry data found for this environment.\")\n89\t  else:\n90\t      4 columns: calls | total_tokens | avg_latency_ms | approx_cost_usd\n91\t```\n92\t\n93\tApproximate cost is computed from total tokens using a conservative constant (`~$0.60/1M tokens` as a placeholder; operator can override). If `total_tokens_sum == 0`, cost shows as `-`.\n94\t\n95\t### DD6 — Logs environment filter\n96\t\n97\tAdd a selectbox before existing filters:\n98\t```python\n99\tenv_options = [\"all\", \"paper\", \"backtest\"]\n100\tlog_env = st.selectbox(\"Environment\", env_options, index=0)\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\tIf `log_env != \"all\"`, apply `.filter(Log.environment == log_env)` to the query.\n104\t\n105\t---\n106\t\n107\t## Position Model Note\n108\t\n109\t`Position` has no `environment` column. The open positions section shows all positions with a caption: _\"Positions are not environment-scoped; showing all open positions.\"_ Adding `environment` to `Position` is out of scope for this ticket.\n110\t\n111\t---\n112\t\n113\t## Degradation Contract\n114\t\n115\tEvery new DB call is wrapped in try/except and returns empty dict/None/[]. Every UI block checks the returned value and shows an explicit `st.info()` message when no data is present. No section may propagate an exception to the Streamlit renderer.\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4ffb124-556a-4a26-b5a1-3a5ae3b4c5ab","uuid":"ffd31d2d-682a-491a-aad7-aba522cd437f","timestamp":"2026-05-13T12:44:39.496Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/03_design/QuantAgent-s62-DS-operational-observability.md","content":"# Design: Extend Minimal Operational Observability\n\n**Issue:** QuantAgent-s62  \n**Related:** [RQ](../01_requirements/QuantAgent-s62-RQ-operational-observability.md) | [PL](../02_planning/QuantAgent-s62-PL-operational-observability.md) | [AC](../05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-s62-AC-operational-observability.md)\n\n---\n\n## Level of Detail\n\n**STANDARD** — UI-layer wiring of existing primitives; no new persistence or models required.\n\n---\n\n## Affected Components\n\n- `quantagent/llm_telemetry.py` — new aggregation function\n- `apps/streamlit/services/db.py` — new DbHandle method\n- `apps/streamlit/views/dashboard.py` — wire placeholder\n- `apps/streamlit/views/paper_trading.py` — two new sections\n- `apps/streamlit/views/logs.py` — environment filter\n\n---\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### DD1 — Reuse existing primitives, no new tables\n\n`QuantAgent-69d` already persists `llm_call` log rows with `environment`, `extra_data` (tokens, duration), and `event_type`. The new `get_environment_metrics()` function filters on these fields. This requires no migrations.\n\n`QuantAgent-vje` already defines `SchedulerHeartbeat` model and `DbHandle.get_latest_heartbeat()`. The dashboard wiring is pure UI: replace placeholder text with a call to the existing method.\n\n### DD2 — `get_environment_metrics()` in `llm_telemetry.py`\n\n```python\ndef get_environment_metrics(\n    db: Any,\n    environment: str,\n    hours_back: int = 24,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n```\n\n- Queries `Log` rows: `event_type='llm_call'`, `environment=environment`, `timestamp >= now - hours_back hours`.\n- Delegates to `_aggregate_rows()` (reuse existing).\n- Returns same shape as `get_session_metrics()`: `{calls, input_tokens_sum, output_tokens_sum, total_tokens_sum, duration_ms_sum, duration_ms_avg, by_operation}`.\n\n### DD3 — `DbHandle.get_paper_llm_metrics()`\n\nThin wrapper in `db.py` to keep the view layer clean:\n\n```python\ndef get_paper_llm_metrics(self, environment: str, hours_back: int = 24) -> dict:\n    if not self.ok:\n        return {}\n    try:\n        from quantagent.llm_telemetry import get_environment_metrics\n        with self.SessionLocal() as session:\n            return get_environment_metrics(session, environment, hours_back)\n    except Exception:\n        return {}\n```\n\n### DD4 — Dashboard scheduler status wiring\n\nThe Dashboard's \"Scheduler Status\" placeholder gets replaced with an inline snippet that calls `db.get_latest_heartbeat(environment)` and renders status/last-run. Helper functions `_calculate_status()` and `_humanize_time()` are duplicated inline (3 lines each) in dashboard.py to avoid creating a shared utils file for this single usage — consistent with AGENTS.md \"minimum needed for the current task.\"\n\n### DD5 — Paper Trading tab extensions\n\nTwo new `st.divider()` + section blocks are appended after the existing `_render_recent_runs()` call in `render()`:\n\n**Block A — Positions, Orders & PnL:**\n```\n[Divider]\nst.subheader(\"Positions & Orders\")\n  col: open positions table (Position model — all, no env filter)\n  col: recent orders table (Order filtered by environment, limit 20)\n[Divider]\nst.subheader(\"PnL Summary\")\n  unrealized PnL from positions\n  daily realized PnL from trades (today, filtered by environment)\n```\n\n**Block B — LLM Cost & Latency:**\n```\n[Divider]\nst.subheader(\"LLM Cost & Latency (last 24h)\")\n  metrics = db.get_paper_llm_metrics(environment)\n  if metrics.get(\"calls\", 0) == 0:\n      st.info(\"No LLM telemetry data found for this environment.\")\n  else:\n      4 columns: calls | total_tokens | avg_latency_ms | approx_cost_usd\n```\n\nApproximate cost is computed from total tokens using a conservative constant (`~$0.60/1M tokens` as a placeholder; operator can override). If `total_tokens_sum == 0`, cost shows as `-`.\n\n### DD6 — Logs environment filter\n\nAdd a selectbox before existing filters:\n```python\nenv_options = [\"all\", \"paper\", \"backtest\"]\nlog_env = st.selectbox(\"Environment\", env_options, index=0)\n```\n\nIf `log_env != \"all\"`, apply `.filter(Log.environment == log_env)` to the query.\n\n---\n\n## Position Model Note\n\n`Position` has no `environment` column. The open positions section shows all positions with a caption: _\"Positions are not environment-scoped; showing all open positions.\"_ Adding `environment` to `Position` is out of scope for this ticket.\n\n---\n\n## Degradation Contract\n\nEvery new DB call is wrapped in try/except and returns empty dict/None/[]. Every UI block checks the returned value and shows an explicit `st.info()` message when no data is present. No section may propagate an exception to the Streamlit renderer.\n","numLines":116,"startLine":1,"totalLines":116}}}
